WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.173
Gate 9's proof isn't a one-time run;

2
00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:05.438
it's a set of standing
checks on the drift cadence.

3
00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.423
For the HR track, the
uncorrelated accounts,

4
00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:11.326
the counts per code
and the duplicate keys.

5
00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:13.764
For groups and units, membership swings,

6
00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:17.163
paused processing and unit
rules against their groups.

7
00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:21.002
Each track also runs its own
standing checks in its own guide:

8
00:00:21.002 --> 00:00:25.993
devices missing their provisioning
attributes and stale devices for Intune,

9
00:00:25.993 --> 00:00:29.756
seven checks for Arc servers
from tags to role assignments,

10
00:00:29.756 --> 00:00:34.363
and owners, credentials and AI agent
sponsors for non-person identities.

11
00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:37.478
The commands differ by
track: delegated for HR,

12
00:00:37.478 --> 00:00:41.987
certificate-based for Intune, Reader
on the subscriptions for Arc.

13
00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:47.274
Behind them sits the workbook's verification
list, ending in zero drift findings.

14
00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:49.037
This gate has no rollback.

15
00:00:49.037 --> 00:00:50.450
It's the standing loop.
